      "severity_calibration": "Medium-High. The duplicate column attack enables a peer to cause the server to perform maximum-bounded work (storage lookups, stream writes) for minimum unique data. On mainnet with MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars=16384, this allows 16384 storage operations and stream writes per request per connection. Under connection flooding, this constitutes a DoS amplification attack bounded only by the rate limiter (which is incorrectly charged based on duplicates).",
