    "phase1": {
      "abstract_interpretation": "The function iterates blocks (outer loop) and sidecars (inner loop), decrementing quota after each sidecar write. The early-exit condition 'if quota == 0 { return 0, nil }' is evaluated INSIDE the inner sidecar loop. This means quota can reach zero after streaming k < len(wantedDataColumnIndices) sidecars for a block, leaving the remainder unstreamned. The requesting peer receives a partial set for that block.",
      "invariants_identified": [
        "quota decrements per-sidecar (not per-block)",
        "Early exit occurs inside inner loop (mid-block)",
        "Spec intent: if a block is included, ALL requested columns for it must be included"
      ]
    },
    "phase2": {
      "symbolic_execution": "Concrete trace: MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars=10, wantedColumns=[0,1,2,3] (4 columns). Block A: streams 4 sidecars (quota: 10->6). Block B: streams 4 sidecars (quota: 6->2). Block C: streams column[0] (quota: 2->1), streams column[1] (quota: 1->0) -> EARLY EXIT. Result: peer receives columns [0,1] for Block C but not [2,3]. Peer cannot reconstruct Block C data reliably.",
      "counterexamples": [
        {
          "scenario": "Quota exhaustion mid-block",
          "inputs": "MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars=10, request.Columns=[0,1,2,3], Count >= 3 blocks each with 4 available sidecars",
          "outcome": "Block C receives only columns 0 and 1 instead of all 4 requested. Violation of atomicity per block."
        }
      ]
    },
    "phase2_5": {
      "additional_vectors": "Any peer can craft a request to trigger this: choose Count and Columns such that MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars % len(Columns) != 0. The 3rd-to-last block will always receive a partial sidecar set.",
      "attack_surface": "Peer requesting data may receive incomplete sidecar set per block, making erasure coding reconstruction impossible for the partial block."
    },
    "phase3": {
      "invariant_proving": "The invariant 'all sidecars for included block must be served' FAILS. Proof: Let N = MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars, K = len(wantedColumns). If N mod K != 0, then after floor(N/K) complete blocks, the (floor(N/K)+1)th block will have only (N mod K) sidecars served. This is a provably reachable state for any K that does not evenly divide N.",
      "proof_or_counterexample": "N=16384 (mainnet), K=3: 16384 mod 3 = 1. The 5462nd block will receive only 1 out of 3 requested sidecars. Deterministically triggerable."
    },
    "phase3_5": {
      "severity_calibration": "Medium. Causes incomplete sidecar delivery per block. Peers expecting complete data for each block will fail reconstruction. Aligned with Fulu spec requirement that block sidecar delivery must be atomic per block.",
      "exploitability": "Deterministically triggerable by any P2P peer with a correctly crafted request. No authentication needed."
    },
    "final_classification": "vulnerability",
    "bug_bounty_eligible": true,
    "vulnerability_description": "streamDataColumnBatch can return mid-block when quota is exhausted, violating the Fulu spec requirement that if any sidecar for a block is served, all requested sidecars for that block must be served. This is deterministically triggerable when MaxRequestDataColumnSidecars is not evenly divisible by the number of requested columns.",
    "reasoning": "The quota decrement occurs per-sidecar inside the inner loop, with early exit on quota==0 without block-boundary awareness. The Fulu spec requires per-block atomicity of sidecar delivery. This is a confirmed violation.",
    "recommended_fix": "Before beginning to stream sidecars for a block, check if quota >= len(wantedDataColumnIndices). If not, break the outer loop without streaming any sidecars for that block. Change: add a pre-check 'if quota < uint64(len(wantedDataColumnIndices)) { return quota, nil }' before the inner sidecar loop."
